@startuml f8-task-finalization
title F8 — Task finalization (no queues)

|AG|
start
:Agent loop complete;
:Emit final result
 (stdout / exit code);

|EX|
:Capture final stdout + exit code;
:REST POST /events
 to Event Router
 { status=terminal, payload=result };

|ER|
:Persist final event in ER DB;
:UPDATE task SET status=terminal in ER DB;
:Push to subscribers (GW);
:Send webhook to Auto (if configured);

fork
  |API Gateway|
  :Receive final event from ER;
  :Proxy to UI over WS (per F3);
  -->[ws] "Operator sees terminal status"

  |Operator|
  :Receive WS final frame;

  |EX|
  :Stop container
   (SIGTERM, then SIGKILL after grace);
  :Unmount tmpfs (plaintext gone);

fork again
  |ER|
  :Invalidate scope_token cache entry
   in ER DB;
end fork

stop

note right
  Three concurrent cleanup paths
  fan out from a single final event
  pushed by ER.
  GW just proxies the WS frame.
end note

@enduml